# timeline-speed.script -- used by timeline-check.sh section 2 (same tick, three speeds).
# One ledger reading before the capture pin fires: the gate compares the speed the
# run reports against the speed it asked for. Without this line a product that
# played 8x at 4x would still pass the pixel clause (T85 measured: the frame at a
# pinned tick is a pure function of the tick), so this is where the mapping is
# actually observable.
playback-state
# Wait for the capture pin at tick 600; the product quits itself once the frame is
# written (main.cpp:11377-11387). The step never completes, which is correct.
tick 999999
